<title>GREECE: ALICO EUROBANK GROWTH FUND 76PCT INVESTED IN Q1.</title>
<headline>ALICO EUROBANK GROWTH FUND 76PCT INVESTED IN Q1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alico Eurobank growth fund which</p>
<p>ranked seventh out of the group of 27 equity growth funds in the</p>
<p>first quarter with a return of 37.45 percent said it was 76</p>
<p>percent invested.</p>
<p>&quot;With dividend reinvestment the fund has delivered a total</p>
<p>return of 99.2 percent since its launch date -- February 12</p>
<p>1993. The comparable market return for the same period was 66.1</p>
<p>percent,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Its main holdings included shares of OTE telecom ,</p>
<p>National Bank , Alpha Credit Bank , Metka</p>
<p>and Titan Cement.</p>
<p>&quot;The fund took advantage of the market's volatility during</p>
<p>the first quarter. It remained 87 to 92 percent invested during</p>
<p>February but reduced exposure to 80 percent during the market's</p>
<p>correction in March,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>It reported the following asset allocation:</p>
<p>    Banks	   48.0 percent</p>
<p>    Metallurgy    18.0 percent</p>
<p>    Cements	  9.0 percent</p>
<p>    Telecoms	 8.2 percent</p>
<p>    Construction   6.1 percent</p>
<p>    Foods	    5.4 percent</p>
<p>    Small Caps     2.0 percent</p>
<p>    Investment     1.4 percent</p>
<p>    Insurance	1.2 percent</p>
<p>    Chemicals	0.7 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
